      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "去 / 来 + place",
      "body": "To say you go somewhere, put the place right after 去: 去学校 = go to school. To say someone comes somewhere, put the place after 来: 来我家 = come to my home. 去 is movement away from where the speaker is, 来 is movement toward the speaker. No extra word like 'to' is needed.",
